                <pb facs="0637" n="537" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg537"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/6496: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-04T16:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1920—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10:38 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>According to the Czechs, Semenoff forces showing signs of breaking up. It is
                    believed Semenoff will try to escape to Urga in Mongolia. Three thousand
                    Bolshevik troops are reported near station Olovyannaya 60 miles east of Chita.
                    Part of Semenoff troops concentrating at station Dauria near Manchurian
                    frontier. Many Russian officers presumably former Koichak and Semenoff men are
                    straggling into Harbin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
